.TH NEALSD 8 "August 2026" "neals" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
nealsd \- Neals local platform daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nealsd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nealsd
is the background daemon for
.BR neals (1).
It accepts JSON-line requests over a UNIX socket, runs
.B devenv up
/
.B down
for registered projects, globally allocates loopback TCP ports for
.B neals.services.*.port
(preferred start port; next free port if busy), injects
.BI NEALS_ SERVICE _PORT
into the project environment, manages
.B .neals
symlinks for UNIX services, and runs a dedicated Caddy instance that reverse-proxies
services with
.B proxy = true
at
.BI {service}.{project}.localhost .
Legacy
.B neals.route.*
declarations are still accepted.
.PP
Prefer starting it via systemd:
.B nealsd@\fIUSER\fR.service
(see
.IR contrib/systemd/ ).
The CLI also auto-starts an ad-hoc
.B nealsd
when no system socket is present.
.SH SOCKETS
.TP
.I /run/neals/nealsd.sock
System unit (RuntimeDirectory=neals, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/neals/nealsd.sock
Ad-hoc / development.
.PP
Override with
.BR NEALS_SOCKET .
.SH HTTP
.TP
System mode (\fBNEALS_MODE=system\fR)
Listen
.B 127.0.0.1:80
(unit grants
.BR CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE ).
.TP
Ad-hoc
Listen
.B 127.0.0.1:2015
unless
.B NEALS_CADDY_HTTP_ADDR
is set.
.PP
Caddy config and logs live under the state directory
(typically
.IR ~/.local/state/neals/ ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NEALS_MODE
.B system
selects privileged HTTP defaults.
.TP
.B NEALS_CADDY_HTTP_ADDR
Caddy listen address.
.TP
.B NEALS_CADDY_CMD
Override Caddy binary/args, or
.B \-
to disable Caddy (tests).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/neals/projects.json
Registry read by the daemon on up/down.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/neals/caddy.json
Generated Caddy config.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/neals/*.log
Per-project and daemon logs.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/nealsd@.service
Systemd template unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR neals (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR caddy (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Neals contributors.
